<section class="security section" id="security" aria-labelledby="security-title">
  <div class="security__inner">
    <div class="security__copy" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">04 / TRUST THE CONNECTION</p>
      <h2 id="security-title">Connected.<br /><span>Not exposed.</span></h2>
      <p>Companions do not join the workspace just because they are nearby. Pairing is explicit, identity is verified, and every session proves it belongs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="security__panel" data-reveal aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="security__panel-topline"><span>VERIFIED PAIRING</span><span class="status-dot"></span></div>
      <div class="security__code"><span>7</span><span>3</span><span>1</span><span>9</span><span>4</span><span>2</span></div>
      <div class="security__verified"><span class="security__check">✓</span><span>Same code. Same devices.</span></div>
      <div class="security__signal"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="security__principles" data-reveal>
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Approve the pair.</h3><p>Compare a verification code on both devices before a new peer is trusted. Changed keys require a fresh approval.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Protect the session.</h3><p>Nonce-bound possession proofs, authenticated encryption, and replay checks protect commands, frames, and annotations.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Keep the relay blind.</h3><p>The optional rendezvous relay helps encrypted peers connect. It cannot read their payloads.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
